    "text": "{\n  \"semantic_type\": \"flow\",\n  \"unit\": \"USD\",\n  \"additive_over_entities\": true,\n  \"additive_over_time\": false,\n  \"time_rollup\": \"reported_fy_value\",\n  \"valid_methods\": [\"sum_across_entities\", \"ratio_of_sums\", \"pct_change\"],\n  \"period_basis\": \"mixed\",\n  \"derivation\": \"Net cash provided by (used in) operating activities, taken as reported in SEC XBRL filings. Each row covers a Q, YTD6, YTD9 or FY period, so the quarterly rows are cumulative within the fiscal year. Summing rows across periods double-counts, so use the FY row for annual totals. Quarterly figures need differencing of YTD values, and that differencing is not part of this column. The XBRL concept varies by company: most use NetCashProvidedByUsedInOperatingActivities, while DRI uses the ContinuingOperations variant.\",\n  \"calendar\": \"fiscal\",\n  \"seasonal_adjustment\": \"n/a\",\n  \"annualized\": false,\n  \"entity_grain\": \"ticker\",\n  \"hierarchy\": null,\n  \"comparability\": \"by_definition_id\",\n  \"lineage\": {\n    \"source\": \"SEC EDGAR XBRL companyfacts API\",\n    \"url_template\": \"https://data.sec.gov/api/xbrl/companyfacts/CIK{cik}.json\",\n    \"retrieved_on\": \"2026-10-24\"\n  },\n  \"description\": \"Operating cash flow in USD per company and reporting period, from SEC XBRL company facts. Rows cover quarterly, year-to-date (6 and 9 month) and full-fiscal-year durations, so values are not additive over time. Add them across companies only when the period basis matches.\"\n}",
